\begin{proposition}
\label{prop:1.34}
[Closed subspaces of complete spaces are complete]
Let $(X,d)$ be a complete metric space and let $Y\subseteq X$ be a closed subset. Then the metric subspace $(Y,d|_{Y\times Y})$ is complete.
\end{proposition}

proof:
\begin{proof}
\label{prf:prop:1.34}
Let $(y_n)_{n=1}^\infty$ be a Cauchy sequence in $(Y,d|_{Y\times Y})$. Then $(y_n)$ is also a Cauchy sequence in $(X,d)$.

Since $X$ is complete, $(y_n)$ converges to some $x\in X$.

Since $Y$ is closed and $(y_n)$ is a sequence in $Y$ converging to $x$, we have $x\in Y$ (closed sets contain limits of their convergent sequences).

Thus $(y_n)$ converges to $x$ in $(Y,d|_{Y\times Y})$, proving $Y$ is complete.
\end{proof}

